1 CLOSE

   Closes a file OPEN opened, and deassigns its logical name.

   Format

     CLOSE logical-name[:]

2 Parameter

 logical-name[:]

   The name OPEN gave the file.

2 Qualifiers
/ERROR

      /ERROR=label

   In a command procedure, goes to the label if the name names no file
   OPEN opened, or the file can't be closed.

/LOG

      /[NO]LOG

   /NOLOG makes a name that names no file OPEN opened a success, with
   no message.  The default, /LOG, reports it as DCL-W-UNDFIL.

2 Examples

   1.$ CLOSE/NOLOG OUT

     Closes OUT's file, if it is open.
